      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T09:58:08Z",
      "duration_ms": 293000,
      "summary": [
        "Rewrote parseGitCredentials() in src/config/config.ts to accept both old Record<string,string> (auto-migrated) and new GitCredentialEntry[] (validated) formats.",
        "Migration logic converts hostname keys to kebab-case IDs via toKebabCase(), sets label to hostname, preserves host/token. Numeric suffix disambiguation (-2, -3, ...) handles ID collisions.",
        "Validation rejects: duplicate id values, empty id/label/host/token fields, non-object array elements, and non-object/non-array values.",
        "Empty {} legacy config returns undefined (no credentials); [] array returns [] (empty credentials set).",
        "Updated src/tests/config.test.ts: removed 8 outdated tests (old Record format expectations), added comprehensive tests covering migration, idempotency, duplicate ID rejection, empty-field rejection, and disambiguation.",
        "config.dist.json already contains \"gitCredentials\": [] — no change needed.",
        "All 62 tests in config.test.ts pass. No type errors in modified files. Pre-existing type errors in downstream files (server/routes/config.ts, orchestrators) are intentional per WP-001 design — they will be fixed in WP-005 and WP-007."
      ],
      "artifacts": {
        "files_modified": [
          "src/config/config.ts",
          "src/tests/config.test.ts"
        ]
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:58:08Z",
          "note": "parseGitCredentials() in config.ts now imports toKebabCase from utils/slug.ts for hostname-to-ID conversion. This is a clean reuse of the existing utility and is consistent with how slug generation works elsewhere in the codebase."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:58:08Z",
          "note": "The downstream files (src/orchestration/repository-orchestrator.ts, src/orchestration/workspace-orchestrator.ts, src/server/routes/config.ts) still use the old Record<string,string> format via 'this.config.gitCredentials ?? {}', causing type errors that block the full tsc build. These are intentional per the WP-001 design but should be addressed promptly in WP-005 and WP-007 to restore a clean build."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T09:58:08Z",
          "note": "The empty legacy object {} returns undefined (no credentials), while an empty array [] returns [] (credentials explicitly set to empty). This asymmetry is intentional and documented in the JSDoc, but could surprise developers — a comment in the code makes this explicit."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-06-26T09:58:36Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-06-26T10:00:37Z",
      "duration_ms": 121000,
      "summary": [
        "All 8 acceptance criteria verified through code review, unit test execution, and targeted edge-case stress testing. 62/62 tests in config.test.ts pass. No regressions introduced. The parseGitCredentials() implementation is correct and robust."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "62 tests covering all branches: null/undefined, empty array, valid array, duplicate id rejection, empty field rejection, non-object element, legacy migration, kebab-case derivation, label preservation, host preservation, disambiguation with numeric suffix, idempotency, plain string rejection, legacy number/empty-string token rejection",
        "tests_passed": 62,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:00:37Z",
          "note": "Whitespace-only strings (e.g. '   ') are correctly rejected for id, label, host, and token — the trim() check before emptiness validation works as expected."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:00:37Z",
          "note": "Triple (and higher) ID collisions work correctly: 'github.com', 'github-com', 'github_com' all resolve to 'github-com' base slug but emerge as 'github-com', 'github-com-2', 'github-com-3' with full uniqueness."
