        },
        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:02:11Z",
          "note": "A04 / Insecure Design — src/config/config.ts (parseGitCredentials, both paths): The `host` field is accepted as any non-empty string without hostname format validation. A malformed value (e.g. containing path traversal sequences, null bytes, or whitespace) could cause unexpected behaviour in downstream git credential matching (WP-005/WP-007 scope). Recommendation: validate `host` against a basic hostname pattern (e.g. no slashes, no null bytes, must resemble a domain or IP) in a future WP."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-26T10:02:11Z",
          "note": "A02 / Cryptographic Failures (defence-in-depth) — src/config/config.ts:300-302: saveConfigField() correctly applies chmodSync(0o600) after writing config.json on POSIX systems to restrict token file to owner-only read/write. This is a positive security control. Note: on Windows, no equivalent permission restriction is applied — acceptable for a local tool but worth documenting in the README."
        },
